# Shell scripts must always check out with LF endings.
#
# They are executed by bash — Git Bash / WSL during the Windows build
# (e.g. modules/device-protocol build, scripts/patch-electrobun.sh) and by
# macOS/Linux. With core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows clones) and no
# explicit rule, these files arrive as CRLF, which breaks bash parsing and
# fails the Windows preflight check (scripts/preflight-windows.ps1).
*.sh text eol=lf
